+# Optional explicit record writer
+
+This local contribution adds the optional Hermes record-write interface. It
+requires a host with that capability and explicit plugin consent; installing
+the provider patch alone does not activate workflow writes.
+
+The writer uses the provider's existing initialized endpoint, credentials,
+resolved write-bank set, retain tags and extraction strategy. Context-only mode
+opts out. Normal conversation capture, recall and built-in-memory mirroring keep
+their existing behavior. No new model summarizer is involved.
+
+Async retain returns `queued`; synchronous successful retain returns
+`acknowledged`. Partial writes, transport failures and deadlines return `unknown`
+and are never automatically repeated. The capability declares no durable client-ID
+deduplication or receipt lookup, and never claims recall visibility. Existing
+configured mirror banks remain part of the destination; partial fanout requires
+operator reconciliation. The binding is a digest, not a credential or bank label.
